{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/philaDAO/posts/statement-from-da-krasner-a-philadelphia-jury-on-monday-found-41-year-old-mauric/1024667776477075/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/philaDAO/posts/statement-from-da-krasner-a-philadelphia-jury-on-monday-found-41-year-old-mauric/1024667776477075/","title":"Philadelphia District Attorney’s Office","description":"Statement from DA Krasner : \n\nA Philadelphia jury on Monday found 41-year-old Maurice Hill guilty of attempted murder and related aggravated assault charges for his role in a violent standoff with...","language":"en","text":"Statement from DA Krasner :\n\nA Philadelphia jury on Monday found 41-year-old Maurice Hill guilty of attempted murder and related aggravated assault charges for his role in a violent standoff with Philadelphia police officers in August 2019. His reckless disregard for the safety of police and the community resulted in six injured officers and traumatized both the Philadelphia Police Department and nearby Nicetown-Tioga residents. Today's conviction sends a clear message that the Philadelphia District Attorney's Office and our partners strongly condemn violence against police and that wanton disregard for public safety will not be tolerated.\"\n\n\"I want to commend the Philadelphia Police Department for their tremendous bravery on August 14, 2019. I also want to thank Assistant District Attorneys Anthony Voci and Sean Perez for securing justice in this case, the jury for their service, and the Philadelphia District Attorney's Office Victim Services Unit and our community-based victim service organizations for their tireless work addressing the needs of survivors impacted by that dark day.\"\n\nAll reactions:\n\n4 comments\n\n1 share\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nNoctis Ffdisidia\n\nAnd yet still 0 done about Erica C Coklin formally Yatsuk, Obstructing Justice\n\nJohn Burke\n\nWhat's going on Larry? Krasner’s two top handpicked ‘Conviction Integrity Unit' supervisors quit one day after a lawsuit called into question the unit’s practices. Total coincidence, obviously. Nothing says ‘integrity’ like sprinting out the door before the subpoenas show up. Timing is Everything\" KYW - 5/12/25 https://www.audacy.com/kywnewsradio/news/local/da-krasner-loses-top-supervisors-in-conviction-integrity-unit-one-day-after-lawsuit-filed\n\nJohn Burke\n\nUpdate: District Attorney Larry Krasner said it was because they’d done such a great job.\n\n“They’re very much in demand, so both Mr. Garmisa and Carrie Wood, whose private business is not mine to tell you, have very exciting next chapters, very exciting opportunities,” he said.\n\nNeither Garmisa nor Wood could be reached.\n\nMichael Kirn\n\n\"Inky editors turn a blind eye to Larry Krasner's lawlessness\n\nIn endorsing the D.A. for reelection, the Inky ignores overwhelming evidence of Krasner's corruption.\"\n\nRalph Cipriano\n\nMay 5\n\nhttps://open.substack.com/pub/ralphcipriano/p/inky-editors-turn-a-blind-eye-to?utm\\_source=share&utm\\_medium=android&r=599va3\n\n1","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":1655.9776739959489,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}